# PM GitHub Workflow .gitignore

# SECRETS
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.keystore
*.jks
api-keys.md
secrets/
secrets.*
*token*
*secret*
*credential*
credentials.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*-adminsdk*.json
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
id_ed25519
.npmrc
.pypirc
# Belt-and-suspenders only — run a real scanner (gitleaks / trufflehog) in CI.

# OS FILES
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# NODE / NPM
node_modules/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
bun.lockb

# PYTHON
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# LARGE DATA FILES
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
data/raw/
exports/
recordings/
transcripts/raw/
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.wav
*.m4a
*.mov
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# CLAUDE CODE
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/statsig/
# Activated skill copies. The source of truth is skills/; .claude/skills/ is a
# local convenience copy (see README), so it shouldn't be committed twice.
.claude/skills/

# IDE FILES
.vscode/
.cursor/
.idea/
*.code-workspace

# BUILD ARTIFACTS
dist/
build/
out/
*.log
.next/
.vercel/

# PM-SPECIFIC
*.otter
*.granola
drafts/wip/
scratch/
screenshots/
screen-recordings/

# RESEARCH OUTPUTS (often contain customer PII / verbatim quotes)
# These globs catch any file whose name starts with feedback-synthesis or
# competitor- (dated or not) — the skills save dated outputs in that form, but
# we ignore both so a transcript full of customer names can't be committed by
# accident. Want to share a sanitized one? `git add -f <file>`
feedback-synthesis*.md
competitor-*.md
transcripts/
interviews/
*transcript*
*interview*
*-raw.*
data/exports/
# Re-include ONLY the repo's shipped source, so a PII-named output dropped into
# skills/ or evals/ still gets caught (the broad globs above still apply there).
!skills/*/SKILL.md
!evals/*-criteria.md
!evals/how-to-write-eval-criteria.md

# ENTERPRISE NOTE
# Add regulated document types here
# Consider CODEOWNERS for review requirements
# NDA materials should NEVER be in any repo
